  "summary": "Four of the five top-ranked documents directly apply graph neural network message passing over relational graphs to predicting protein molecular function, which is the closest available match to the research question about GNNs applied to protein function. [V0145] (Gupta et al., 2024) achieves the highest reported accuracy of 0.92 on the ProtMap dataset. [V0148] (Brennan et al., 2018) reports F1=0.78 on MetroFlow. [V0147] (Adebayo et al., 2026) reports AUROC=0.71 on ChurnBench. [V0146] (Haddad et al., 2025) reports MAE=0.64 on FireScope. The fifth document [V0158] (Chen et al., 2019) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles (not GNNs) to protein molecular function on FireScope with accuracy 0.62; it is included as the only remaining protein-function candidate, though it does not use a graph neural network method. No candidate documents apply GNNs directly to protein function annotation tasks such as GO term prediction on standard benchmarks (e.g., PDB, UniProt, STRING), so the synthesis is limited to the supplied candidates.",
